optique inspects and edits the per-port OPTIONS files that poudriere and the
ports tree consume, without going through the interactive dialog4 screens.

It resolves a port's effective option set the way the framework does, walking
the poudriere options directories, make.conf and the port's own OPTIONS_*
defaults. A TUI is provided for browsing and toggling options, while the
non-interactive subcommands (notably "scan --json") suit scripting and bulk
audits of a whole options tree.
